answer:
**Props accepted**

`SidebarMenuSubButton` is declared as  

```tsx
React.forwardRef<
  HTMLAnchorElement,
  React.ComponentProps<"a"> & {
    asChild?: boolean;
    size?: "sm" | "md";
    isActive?: boolean;
  }
>
```  

so it receives:

| Prop | Type / description |
|------|---------------------|
| `asChild` | `boolean` – when `true` the component renders a `<Slot>` (from *radix‑ui*) instead of an `<a>` element. Default: `false`. |
| `size` | `"sm" | "md"` – controls the visual size of the button. Default: `"md"`. |
| `isActive` | `boolean` – indicates an active state. |
| `className` | `string` – CSS class names (part of the native `<a>` props). |
| **All other `<a>` attributes** (e.g., `href`, `target`, `rel`, `onClick`, etc.) – passed through via `React.ComponentProps<"a">`. |
| `ref` | forwarded to the underlying element. |

**How the props are used in the render output**

```tsx
const Comp = asChild ? Slot : "a";

return (
  <Comp
    ref={ref}
    data-sidebar="menu-sub-button"
    data-size={size}
    data-active={isActive}
    className={cn(className)}
    {...props}               // spreads the remaining <a> props
  />
);
```

* The component chooses the element to render (`<Slot>` or `<a>`) based on `asChild`【src/components/ui/sidebar.tsx:670-705】.  
* It always adds the attribute `data-sidebar="menu-sub-button"`【src/components/ui/sidebar.tsx:670-705】.  
* The `size` prop is written to `data-size` (e.g., `data-size="sm"` or `"md"`).  
* The `isActive` prop is written to `data-active` (e.g., `data-active="true"`).  
* The supplied `className` is passed through the `cn` utility to build the final class string【src/components/ui/sidebar.tsx:670-705】.  
* All remaining anchor‑specific props (`href`, `onClick`, etc.) are spread onto the rendered element via `{...props}`【src/components/ui/sidebar.tsx:670-705】.  

Thus, `SidebarMenuSubButton` forwards standard anchor props, adds three custom data attributes (`data-sidebar`, `data-size`, `data-active`), conditionally renders as a `<Slot>` or `<a>`, and merges any custom class names.

