**Component:** `FormMessage` (defined in `src/components/ui/form.tsx`).

**How it uses `formMessageId` and renders errors**

```tsx
const FormMessage = React.forwardRef<
  HTMLParagraphElement,
  React.HTMLAttributes<HTMLParagraphElement>
>(({ className, children, ...props }, ref) => {
  const { error, formMessageId } = useFormField();          // ← gets `formMessageId`
  const body = error ? String(error?.message ?? "") : children;

  if (!body) {
    return null;                                          // nothing rendered if no error/children
  }

  return (
    <p
      ref={ref}
      id={formMessageId}                                   // ← applied to the <p>
      className={cn("text-[0.8rem] font-medium text-destructive", className)}
      {...props}
    >
      {body}                                               // error message text
    </p>
  );
});
```

- `useFormField()` supplies `error` and `formMessageId` (`src/components/ui/form.tsx:55‑71`).
- If an error exists, its message (`error.message`) is converted to a string and rendered inside a `<p>` element.
- The `<p>` receives the `id` attribute set to `formMessageId`, allowing it to be referenced by ARIA attributes elsewhere.
- When there is no error (and no children), the component returns `null`, rendering nothing.

